{title: Oh My Darling Clementine}
{artist: Traditional}
{key: C}

{c: Verse 1}
In a [C]cavern, in a canyon, exca[G7]vating for a mine,
Dwelt a [C]miner, forty-niner, and his [G7]daughter Clemen[C]tine.

{c: Chorus}
Oh my [C]darling, oh my darling, oh my [G7]darling Clemen[C]tine,
You are [C]lost and gone for[Am]ever, dreadful [G7]sorry Clemen[C]tine.

{c: Verse 2}
Light she [C]was and like a fairy, and her [G7]shoes were number nine,
Herring [C]boxes without topses, [G7]sandals were for Clemen[C]tine.
